WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.307
When Connect Bike cannot reach the bike, it now says why, in an alert that gives the

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:08.282
way forward.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:14.981
With Bluetooth off, the alert says so in place of the card and the button. Turn it

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:18.064
on, press try again, and the pair button is back.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:29.067
A browser without Web Bluetooth is sent to Chrome or Edge. A page that is not secure

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:34.441
is offered the same page over HTTPS, and is never told to change browser.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:40.704
If the browser's list of bikes will not open, the alert says whether a policy

00:00:40.704 --> 00:00:43.557
blocked it. Try again opens the list again.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:54.557
Each alert fits a phone, a tablet and a desktop, and works by touch and by keyboard.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:04.552
The specs came first. The words were already right, so only the icon checks failed.

00:01:04.552 --> 00:01:08.792
Now one hundred and sixty-eight specs and every unit test pass.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:17.920
Telo Ride 1, from the Telo family, is the focused edition of Telo Ride: one class,

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:19.116
nothing else.

00:01:19.461 --> 00:01:24.413
It pairs with a smart bike at home over Bluetooth, plays the class video, or draws

00:01:24.413 --> 00:01:29.425
the Ibiza Sunset Strip course to music if the rider chooses it, and sets the bike's

00:01:29.425 --> 00:01:32.926
resistance for every interval while the rider pedals.

00:01:33.272 --> 00:01:37.247
Connect the bike, take the class, see your number, and come back to beat it.
